The writable device open is `O_RDWR | O_EXCL`. O_EXCL on a regular file is a
Linux no-op, but Cosmopolitan's NT open() rejects it with EINVAL ("open failed:
…, Invalid argument" → "exFAT format fail!"). O_EXCL only matters for block
devices, which Windows images are not, so neutralize it under Cosmopolitan (the
same fix as dosfstools; a real-Windows-only failure, wine tolerates it).

--- a/lib/libexfat.c
+++ b/lib/libexfat.c
@@ -12,6 +12,10 @@
 #include <sys/sysmacros.h>
 #include <unistd.h>
 #include <fcntl.h>
+#ifdef __COSMOPOLITAN__
+#undef O_EXCL
+#define O_EXCL 0
+#endif
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <string.h>
